# For staff: the panel

## Open it

Press **Home**, or type `/tickets`.

## The list

- **Age** counts up live.
- A **green** name is online. A **grey, dimmed** row means the player is offline.
- A coloured edge marks **urgent** (red) and **high** (orange).
- Filter with the chips: Open, Claimed, Mine, Closed; the kind; the priority; online only. Search finds names, text, towns and ticket numbers.
- A **red bubble** on a chip or a tab is how many tickets are still waiting behind it. Closed tickets never count.
- **Full screen** at the top right gives you more room. Your choice is remembered on your computer.

You only see the kinds of ticket your role handles, plus any ticket **escalated** to your role. Admins see everything.

## Work a ticket

| Button | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Claim** | It is yours. Everyone else sees your name on it, and the player is told. |
| **Release** | Puts it back for someone else. |
| **Assign** | Gives it to another staff member who handles that kind. |
| **Change kind** | Moves it to the right staff. A Help ticket that is really a bug goes to the developers. |
| **Escalate** | **Adds** another role to the ticket, with a reason. You stay the owner; they can now see it and help. Click the ↑ pill to take it back. |
| **Change priority** | The player cannot change it after sending. You can. |
| **Go to player** / **Go to location** | One press. You arrive a few metres behind them, **invisible and unable to be hurt**. |
| **Return** | Takes you back to where you were, and makes you visible again. |
| **Close ticket** | Pick why. The note is read by the player. |
| **Archive** | Hides the ticket from every list but the **Archived** filter. Nothing is deleted; **Bring back** undoes it. |

Reply in the **Conversation** box when you do not need to go in person. Your messages are on the right, the player's on the left.

- **Internal note**: flip the switch beside the reply box. The box turns dark red, and what you send is for staff only. **The player never receives it.** Use it for hand-offs: what you tried, what you think it is.
- **Ready-made replies** sit above the box. The ones that match what the player wrote come first; **Replies …** shows them all. Picking one fills the box, so you can still change it.
- **Mark as the answer**: hover a message and click it. The answer is pinned in green for you and the player.
- **Make public**: on a closed ticket with a marked answer. Every player can then read it with the names hidden. Read the text first: the names are hidden for you, but make sure nobody is named *in* a message. Tickets about a player can never be made public.

If you log off with a ticket claimed, it shows "staff offline" and frees itself after a while.

## Warn, kick or ban someone: three ways in

You do not need a ticket.

1. **`/mod`** opens the **Players menu**. `/mod 12` opens it on player 12.
2. In the panel, the **Players** tab. On a ticket, click a player's name, or **Record**.
3. In `/poggy`: Tickets → **Players: warn, kick, ban** → **Open the Players menu**. You can also warn, kick and ban straight from that list.

The menu shows everyone online. Pick one to see their record: warnings, bans, and tickets. Then **Go to**, **Warn**, **Kick** or **Ban**.

Someone already left? Type their name in the search box and press **Enter**. Admins can still ban them; anyone with Warn can leave a warning they will see when they log in.

## Reported players

On tickets that name a player:

- **Warn**: they get a full-screen warning they must acknowledge. It is counted on their record.
- **Kick**: removes them now.
- **Ban**: pick how long, and tick "This is for cheating" when it is. The ban is on their account, so it follows them across characters. It works even if they have already left.

Every one needs a reason. The player is **never** told who reported them.

Which of these you get is up to your role.

On a player's record you also see:

- **What the ladder suggests** for their next offence. It is only a suggestion: you decide.
- Old warnings marked **no longer counts**. They stay on the record, but the ladder ignores them.
- **Staff notes**, in dark red: not a warning, never shown to the player. "Rude, not ban-worthy."
- **Watch**: staff who keep notes get a pop-up when that player logs in.

## Help requests

They show in a strip at the top. Press **Responding** so nobody else goes too, then **Go to player**. Press **Done** when it is sorted.

## Duty

The switch at the top right, or `/staffduty`. Off duty: no sounds, no pop-ups, no badge. You are **always back on duty after a relog**, so you cannot forget it off.

## `/invis`

Turns invisibility on or off by hand. It is logged.

## Staff chat

The **Staff chat** tab. You see your own role's room and any room your role may read. It is **never saved**: everything is gone at the next restart. A room marked *Discord* is copied to a Discord channel.

## Admin tabs

- **Bans**: every ban, with **Lift ban**. Lifting needs a reason and keeps the record.
- **Staff**: search any character, online or not, and give them roles. With the power to manage: **Roles** (make your own) and **Ready-made replies**.
- **Audit**: everything staff did, as a timeline grouped by day. Filter by area (Tickets, Moderation, Movement, Staff), by person, or search. Click a ticket number to see only that ticket; **History** on a ticket does the same.
